# Vandeta MITM test payload - a self-contained page, nothing is forwarded.
#
# Use it to prove the attack path end to end:
#   WiFi > Wifi Atks > MITM Attack > Payload > Pick payload > test.mitm
#   Network > pick the AP, Target > All devices (or one host), Start attack
#   then open a plain-HTTP site on the victim, e.g. http://neverssl.com/
#   or the IP literal http://1.1.1.1/ (no DNS needed).
#
# Expected on the victim: the page below, served by the board itself.
# BACK stops the attack and restores every ARP mapping it changed.

# Serve the test page for every plain-HTTP request.
page * html/test.html

# Answer every DNS A query with the gateway. Its MAC is already the board's
# (the ARP poison), so the client's next HTTP request comes here.
dns * gateway

# If nothing lands in 10 s, answer DNS with the gateway instead. This is the
# cascade the deleted rickroller script used.
fallback dns gateway 10
